# MoE OTD perf counters: evictions, acquisitions, slot tiers, staging bytes
#
# Extends the existing [OTD_PERF] runtime counters (MOE_OTD_PERF_LOG=1) with
# what M9's later patches (0005-0007) need to be measured, and moves the
# counter struct into its own header (moe_otd_perf.hpp) so compile-time code
# in a different CMake target can update it without pulling in
# moe_otd_runtime.hpp's cldnn graph/runtime prelude. Applied against the
# pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of patches/0003.
#
# Review-round fix: OtdPerfCounters::dump() printed through GPU_DEBUG_INFO,
# which is gated on ExecutionConfig::get_verbose() >= LogLevel::INFO (1);
# MOE_OTD_PERF_LOG=1 defaults verbose to 0, so the counters collected but the
# line never printed in any of our runs. Switched to GPU_DEBUG_COUT
# (LogLevel::DISABLED = 0), the same get_verbose_stream() channel with the
# verbose check trivially satisfied (get_verbose() >= 0 always), so the env
# var alone is the opt-in, as it was meant to be. dump() runs from a
# std::atexit handler registered inside get_perf_counters() (this plugin's
# .so, not the host binary); that is only safe if the .so is still mapped
# when the handler fires, which holds under our serving pattern — arcint
# loads the GPU plugin once per process and keeps it loaded for the process's
# whole life, so it is never dlclose()'d ahead of exit for the handler to
# outlive. A plugin that could be unloaded mid-run would need a different
# mechanism.
#
# New counters, all in OtdPerfCounters (printed by [OTD_PERF] at process
# exit) unless noted:
#   evictions          - LRUCache evictions, all offloaded MoE layers combined
#                         (lru_cache.cpp:evict_one_unlocked). This is the red-
#                         first observable docs/design-m9-offload-v2.md §1's
#                         P3 paragraph is decided on: at ratio 10 it should
#                         read close to 0 [to measure] since a miss there is
#                         almost certainly compulsory, not a capacity miss.
#   acquisitions       - LRUCache::get_lru_item calls (hits + misses), kept
#                         independent of gpu_hits/gpu_misses so the two
#                         accounting paths can be cross-checked.
#   device_slot_buffers,
#   host_slot_buffers,
#   alloc_fallbacks    - declared here, populated by patches/0005 (P1) at
#                         compile time in try_prepare_partial_upload. Zero on
#                         this patch alone; wiring them here rather than
#                         there keeps 0005's diff to the allocation decision.
#   staging_bytes      - declared here, populated by patches/0006 (P2)'s
#                         staging ring.
#
# The partial-upload compile-stage log (PartialUploadLogState::log,
# src/plugin/ops/moe_offload_constant.cpp/.hpp) gains an alloc= field; it
# prints "usm_host" for every constant until patches/0005 gives it something
# else to print. `grep alloc=usm_device` on that log is the build check
# patches/0005 uses to tell a patched binary from an unpatched one. That log
# line still goes through GPU_DEBUG_INFO, unlike dump() above - it is a
# compile-stage message, not a MOE_OTD_PERF_LOG=1 runtime print, and was not
# reported as silent in the on-GPU pass, so it is left alone here.
#
# Measurement discipline: this patch adds instrumentation only, no behaviour
# change on any code path. Per the design's own gate ("any t/s delta - an
# instrument that costs is not an instrument"), that claim is owed a same-
# seed decode comparison against an unpatched build; not run here — this
# patch was built (CPU-only, ninja) but never loaded onto a GPU device, per
# this task's rules. The orchestrator's on-GPU pass is what discharges it.
